FutureOS: let the privileged SMS app hold the RCS/IMS permissions.

On Android 12 these are internal|role and only the SYSTEM_SHELL role grants
them, so no messaging app can open a SipDelegate. Adding "privileged" lets
com.future.messages get them through its privapp-permissions allowlist.

Apply in frameworks/base:  git apply <this file>

--- a/core/res/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/core/res/AndroidManifest.xml
@@
     <permission android:name="android.permission.PERFORM_IMS_SINGLE_REGISTRATION"
-        android:protectionLevel="internal|role" />
+        android:protectionLevel="internal|role|privileged" />
@@
     <permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_RCS_USER_CAPABILITY_EXCHANGE"
-        android:protectionLevel="internal|role" />
+        android:protectionLevel="internal|role|privileged" />
